<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">San people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bushmen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The San are indigenous hunter-gatherer peoples of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, living today mainly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> and speaking click languages of several families. Their rock art spans thousands of years. Colonial expansion in the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries brought frontier wars in which many were killed or forced into servitude, and some missions, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippolis">Philippolis</a>, were founded for them.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/san-people.jpg" alt="San people" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Velatrix · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Namibian_Bushmen_Girls.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Mellet holds that a proto-Khoe people emerged between 400 BCE and 100 CE in southern Zimbabwe, and also in northern Botswana and along the Limpopo, as the <b>San peoples</b> Tshua and Khwe met herding communities drifting slowly south from East Africa.</blockquote><a href="/culture/khoekhoe">Khoekhoe · Origins</a></li><li><blockquote>Graaff-Reinet, the eastern frontier district of the Dutch Cape Colony, was in turmoil over the Company's handling of conflict with the Xhosa and the <b>San</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/graaff-reinet-republic">Graaff-Reinet Republic</a></li><li><blockquote>Philippolis began in 1823 as a London Missionary Society station for <b>San</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/philippolis-griqua-state">Philippolis Griqua State</a></li></ul></section>
